# Rails conventions

- Follow standard Rails MVC organization.
- Prefer Turbo Streams and Rails helpers over custom JavaScript for interactive UI.
- Keep migrations reversible.
- Use strong parameters for all controller input.
- Use `bin/rails generate` when adding Rails boilerplate such as models, migrations, and controllers.
- Keep changes scoped to the todo app.
- Do not import unrelated models, migrations, or patterns from other projects.
- Keep controller actions small and move repeated view markup into partials.
- Add or update tests for behavior changes.